<section class="rows wrap" id="features">
  <h2 class="vh" data-i18n="rows.h">What Keygloss does</h2>

  <article class="frow">
    <div class="ftext">
      <span class="seq" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="sp"></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span class="bubble"><s>ghbdtn</s> → привет</span>
      <div><h3 data-i18n="r1.h">fixed by the time you hit space</h3>
      <p data-i18n="r1.p">type ghbdtn, press space, and the word becomes привет. the layout switches too, so the next word comes out right the first time.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="win fwin"><div class="win-bar"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="t" data-i18n="ui.pageLayout">Layout switching</span></div>
      <div class="wall"><div class="inner">
        <div class="kgp">
          <div class="row"><span data-i18n="ui.auto">Automatic layout correction</span><i class="tg"></i></div>
          <div class="row"><span data-i18n="ui.fly">Fix as you type</span><i class="tg"></i></div>
          <div class="row"><span data-i18n="ui.short">Shortest word to fix</span><span class="sel">2</span></div>
        </div></div>
        <span class="crop lay trig tilt-r" style="--s:.39" role="img" aria-label="Triggers: after a word, on Space and Enter" data-i18n-attr="aria-label:alt.trig"></span>
      </div></div>
  </article>

  <article class="frow flip">
    <div class="ftext">
      <span class="seq" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i class="sp"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i></span>
      <span class="bubble"><span class="kc">Ctrl</span>+<span class="kc">Alt</span></span>
      <div><h3 data-i18n="r2.h">or do it yourself with one hotkey</h3>
      <p data-i18n="r2.p">Ctrl + Alt switches the text by hand, and undoes a fix you did not want. keygloss can learn from what you undo. the hotkey is yours to change.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="win fwin"><div class="win-bar"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="t" data-i18n="ui.pageLayout">Layout switching</span></div>
      <div class="wall b">
        <span class="photo tilt-l"><span class="crop lay hot" style="--s:.63" role="img" aria-label="The hotkey setting: Ctrl + Alt" data-i18n-attr="aria-label:alt.hot"></span></span>
        <div class="inner"><div class="kgp">
          <div class="row"><span data-i18n="ui.manual">Manual switch and undo</span><span class="sel"><span class="keys"><span class="kc">Ctrl</span>+<span class="kc">Alt</span></span></span></div>
          <div class="row"><span data-i18n="ui.learnUndo">Learn from undo</span><i class="tg"></i></div>
          <div class="row"><span data-i18n="ui.learnSwitch">Learn from switch</span><i class="tg"></i></div>
          <div class="row"><span data-i18n="ui.arrows">Arrow keys cancel the switch</span><i class="tg"></i></div>
        </div></div>
      </div></div>
  </article>

  <article class="frow">
    <div class="ftext">
      <span class="seq" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="sp"></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span class="bubble"><span data-i18n="ui.br">br</span> → <span data-i18n="ui.regards">Best regards, Alex</span></span>
      <div><h3 data-i18n="r3.h">snippets for what you type every day</h3>
      <p data-i18n="r3.p">give a phrase a short abbreviation, type it, and it expands into the full text. layout and case do not matter: !test, !TEST and !еуые are the same snippet.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="win fwin"><div class="win-bar"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="t" data-i18n="ui.pageSnip">Snippets</span></div>
      <div class="wall c2">
        <span class="crop snp ex tilt-l" style="--s:.485" role="img" aria-label="Example snippets: !em, !ph, !adr, !web" data-i18n-attr="aria-label:alt.ex"></span>
        <span class="crop snp greet tilt-r" style="--s:.425" role="img" aria-label="A snippet named Greeting with its text" data-i18n-attr="aria-label:alt.greet"></span>
      </div></div>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="privacy center" id="privacy">
  <div class="arc" id="arcL" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="arc" id="arcR" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <span class="eyebrow" data-i18n="priv.eyebrow">100% local</span>
  <h2 class="vh" data-i18n="priv.h">Privacy: everything stays on this computer</h2>
  <div class="notes win" style="text-align:left">
    <div class="win-bar"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="t" data-i18n="priv.title">notes</span></div>
    <div class="notes-body">
      <p data-i18n="priv.p1">keygloss has to read your keystrokes to fix them, so here is exactly where they go: nowhere.</p>
      <p data-i18n="priv.p2">your typing is processed on this computer only. there is no usage data and no telemetry.</p>
      <p data-i18n="priv.p3">typed text is never logged. <mark>the only text it can keep is the history of recent automatic fixes, and that stays on this computer.</mark></p>
      <p data-i18n="priv.p4">it goes online to check github for a newer release on startup, and when you click a link. nothing else.</p>
      <p><span data-i18n="priv.p5">the startup check can be turned off in settings → general.</span><span class="caret"></span></p>
      <div class="sig"><img src="img/icon.png" alt=""><span><strong>xArchange1,</strong><span data-i18n="priv.role">developer</span></span><span class="hand" aria-hidden="true">keygloss</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

