<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap center">
    <span class="eyebrow">faq</span>
    <h2 data-i18n="faq.h">frequently asked questions</h2>
    <p class="sub" data-i18n="faq.sub">what to know about keygloss, privacy, and getting started.</p>
    <span class="photo" aria-hidden="true"><span class="crop snp sc" style="--s:.33"></span></span>
    <div class="qa" style="text-align:left">
      <details open><summary data-i18n="q1">what is keygloss?</summary><p data-i18n="a1">a small app for windows, macos and linux that fixes text typed in the wrong keyboard layout. type ghbdtn and you get привет, and the layout switches to match. it works between russian and english, as you type or with a hotkey.</p></details>
      <details><summary data-i18n="q2">does it send what i type anywhere?</summary><p data-i18n="a2">no. typing is processed on this computer only. keygloss collects no usage data and has no telemetry, and typed text is never written to its log.</p></details>
      <details><summary data-i18n="q3">when does it connect to the internet?</summary><p data-i18n="a3">on startup, to check github for a newer release, and when you click a link in the app. the startup check can be turned off in settings → general.</p></details>
      <details><summary data-i18n="q4">what does it remember?</summary><p data-i18n="a4">only the history of recent automatic fixes, and only if you turn it on. it is stored on this computer and stays there.</p></details>
      <details><summary data-i18n="q5">what if it changes a word i meant?</summary><p data-i18n="a5">press Ctrl + Alt to undo the fix. you can also mark a word “never translate” in history, or add an app to the exceptions so keygloss stays out of it.</p></details>
      <details><summary data-i18n="q6">which languages does it work with?</summary><p data-i18n="a6">it converts between the russian and english layouts. the app's own interface is available in english and russian.</p></details>
      <details><summary data-i18n="q7">which systems does it run on?</summary><p data-i18n="a7">windows, macos and linux. the linux build is experimental and made for kde plasma 6 on wayland. there is no mobile version.</p></details>
      <details><summary data-i18n="q8">is it free?</summary><p data-i18n="a8">yes. keygloss is free and open source under the mit licence. if it saves you time, you can <a href="https://boosty.to/xarchange1/donate">sponsor the project</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary data-i18n="q9">how does it update?</summary><p data-i18n="a9">from github releases. you choose between the stable and the beta channel in settings. on linux the app tells you about a new release and opens its page.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
